  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed development, by reason of its altered elevational treatment, increased upper floor massing and failure to continue the established architectural language of the host building and surrounding Talina Centre estate, would appear incongruous and visually discordant within its context. Whilst there is a somewhat similar fallback scheme approved at appeal in 2024, that scheme was assessed under the prior approval provisions of Part 20 Class AC of the GPDO where only limited prescribed matters fell to be considered. By contrast, the current proposal must be assessed against the development plan as a whole, including the full design, townscape and character objectives of applicable planning policies. As such, the scheme is contrary to Policies DC1 and DC2 of the Local Plan (2018) and Policy D4 of the London Plan (2021), as well as the National Planning Policy Framework (2024).",
    "Reason : 2 - In the absence of a completed and effective legal agreement and/or Unilateral Undertaking under Section 16 of the Greater London Council (General Powers) Act 1974 securing the relinquishment of the existing external parking space associated with Unit 14 and restricting future occupiers from obtaining on-street parking permits, the Local Planning Authority is not satisfied that the proposed parking mitigation would be secured in perpetuity. Consequently, the proposal fails to demonstrate that it would not result in increased parking demand, adverse impacts on highway conditions, traffic generation, sustainable transport objectives, pedestrian and cyclist safety, or local air quality. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies CC10 and T4 of the Hammersmith & Fulham Local Plan (2018) and Policies T2 and T6 of the London Plan (2021)."
  ],
